I reviewed the Phase R1 changes against `docs/design/dao.runtime.implementation-plan.md`. Here is my report.

## Verdict

The `dao.runtime` Phase R1 implementation **conforms to the plan**. The poll/ready split is implemented as specified, the discarded-poll regression is covered, classification is now declaration-driven, the `gap` adapter rule has its test, and the namespace docstring now states the contract. All requirements in the Phase R1 section are present.

The only problem I found is **out-of-scope**: `docs/agents/team.md` is modified in the same working tree but is unrelated to Phase R1.

## Verification performed

- `clojure -M:test -n dao.runtime-test -n yin.vm.runtime-adapter-test` → 16 tests, 79 assertions, 0 failures.
- `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.engine-test` → 14 tests, 58 assertions, 0 failures (confirms the engine is unaffected by `run-once` no longer polling, as the plan predicted).
- Full `yin.vm` suite (ast-walker, engine, ffi, module, parity, runtime-adapter, stream-observer) → 87 tests, 334 assertions, 0 failures.
- Node/cljs `shadow-cljs compile test` → 1314 tests, 34692 assertions, 0 failures (includes the v2 namespaces).
- I did **not** run the cljd lane; the plan's deliverable includes it, so that remains unverified here.

## Requirement-by-requirement

| Phase R1 item | Status |
|---|---|
| `run-once` pops/resumes head iff `:resume`, never polls | ✅ `src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:247-259` |
| `run-loop` drains ready queue, polls once, continues only if the poll moved something, returns the state holding a host-owned head | ✅ `run-loop` at `:262-282`; the wait-set-count comparison is an accurate "moved" test given `check-wait-set` only moves wait-set → ready-queue |
| Regression test for the discarded poll (fake writer full-once-then-ok, append counter, host-owned head) | ✅ `run-loop-returns-a-polled-state-behind-a-host-owned-head-test` — asserts exactly one append, writer behind the host entry, and both present in the returned state |
| Classification driven by `dao.stream/outcomes-next` / `outcomes-append`, exactly `blocked`/`full` wait, unknown outcome terminal | ✅ `read-expectations`/`write-expectations` + the two classification tests, including the `set (keys …)` coverage guard |
| `gap` carries recovery cursor; adapter stores it | ✅ `gap-wake-replaces-the-stored-cursor-with-the-recovery-cursor-test` |
| Docstring is the contract | ✅ `src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:1-60` |

## Issues

1. **Out-of-scope change: `docs/agents/team.md`** — The diff edits the roster table (QA fallbacks, Routine Review fallbacks, Scoped/Subagent primary) and de-aligns the Routine Review row. This has nothing to do with Phase R1 and is not mentioned anywhere in the implementation plan. It should be reverted or moved to a separate change so this phase's diff contains only the runtime/test changes.

2. *(Cosmetic, tied to #1)* The Routine Review row in `team.md` now has a very long, misaligned fallback cell and trailing spacing inconsistency on the Compiler & AST row. Not worth fixing within this phase unless #1 is kept.

No functional defects were found in the `dao.runtime` source or the new tests.
